#: includes/features/class-rest-for-users.php:55
msgid "Core REST API only for logged-in users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-rest-for-users.php:64
msgid "Visitors who are not logged in get \"You are not currently logged in\" from the core REST API routes (/wp-json/wp/v2/...). Without this anyone can read the list of posts, pages and categories through the API, and /wp-json/wp/v2/media lists the address of every uploaded file, also files that no page links to, like a PDF you uploaded but never published. Fewer open routes also means fewer places where the next core bug can be used. oEmbed and the routes of plugins stay open: forms, shops and statistics keep working. Logged-in users, the block editor and application passwords are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-rest-for-users.php:73
msgid "A headless front end (Next.js, Gatsby, a mobile app) that reads posts through the API without logging in stops getting them, and so does a theme or plugin that loads posts in the visitor's browser through /wp/v2/ (\"load more\" buttons, live search, post sliders). If something on the site stops loading for visitors, add its route below. Plugin routes are not closed, so a plugin with its own security hole is not covered by this."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-rest-for-users.php:82
msgid "Turn this off and save. The routes answer visitors again at once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-rest-for-users.php:120
msgid "Keep open for visitors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-rest-for-users.php:123
msgid "Core routes your visitors need, separated by commas, for example: /wp/v2/posts, /wp/v2/search. A route also opens everything under it (/wp/v2/posts opens /wp/v2/posts/123). Usually empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-security-headers.php:93
msgid "Security headers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-security-headers.php:100
msgid "Adds four headers: X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff (browsers do not guess file types), X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN (other sites cannot show your pages in a frame), Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin (other sites see only your domain, not full URLs) and Permissions-Policy (your pages and anything embedded in them cannot use motion sensors, USB devices, or the browser features you do not tick below)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-security-headers.php:107
msgid "If your pages are shown inside a frame on another domain, for example in a landing page builder or on a partner site, they stop opening there. If you leave a box below unticked but the site uses it, that part stops working: Apple Pay and Google Pay buttons, \"find stores near me\", video calls. Tilting the phone to look around 360° videos stops working. The editor and the Customizer are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-security-headers.php:114
msgid "Turn this off and save. Browsers drop these headers on the next page load. If the server or another plugin also sends them, those copies stay."
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-security-headers.php:202
msgid "Quick payment buttons (Apple Pay, Google Pay, Link)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-security-headers.php:203
msgid "Visitor location (store locator, \"near me\" search, map with \"my location\")"
msgstr ""

#: includes/features/class-security-headers.php:204
msgid "Camera and microphone (video calls, recording in the browser)"
msgstr ""

